#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:5
#: 3ca6023efea14b04bda2bd7e3354184c
msgid "Return to Launch"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:7
#: 159da1403c2c45daad7704c054d6caad
msgid "Returning to Launch (either HOME or a Rally point) can be executed by either switching to RTL mode or QRTL mode. In each case a key concept is the return point. This is defined as the closest rally point, or if a rally point is not defined, then the HOME location. See the :ref:`Rally Points <common-rally-points>` page for more information on rally points."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:12
#: bffa1d9895d142d3b76bc795c795ffd3
msgid "RTL mode has four different options for its behavior but basically uses fixed wing flight for at least the majority of the return. Behavior also depends on how close to the return point the vehicle is when entered and from what mode, fixed wing or VTOL/QAssist. RTL mode behavior is determined by the :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` parameter and explained in the sections below."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:14
#: 8908b21a22084eb68a1feba703e69d22
msgid "QRTL mode, by default, will return either in fixed wing mode and land in VTOL mode the same way as the RTL mode selected by :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` = 3, or by using :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit (16), as a pure VTOL return and land."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:16
#: a4efa2e19a254b7db007b94769bf2b7d
msgid "RC failsafe when in a VTOL mode will only result in either a switch to QLAND, RTL, or QRTL, depending on the :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 5 (QRTL) and bit 20 (RTL) settings (bit 20 overrides bit 5), independent of what the :ref:`FS_SHORT_ACTN<FS_SHORT_ACTN>` or :ref:`FS_LONG_ACTN<FS_LONG_ACTN>` setting is."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:20
#: 5974351eae7143f89151389108e47bd8
msgid "RTL Modes"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:22
#: 0d6b6efcfd9c4439b3890523b818474e
msgid "Fixed Wing RTL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:25
#: 1ac291910ba547d1820a84235882497a
msgid ":ref:`Q_RTL_MODE <Q_RTL_MODE>` = 0"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:26
#: 3d15135007f74a01907bf35c35eaaa4f
msgid "**RETURN FIXED WING AND LOITER**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:28
#: 17c08d38feb242b1a2d47be56ad70506
msgid "The default behaviour (:ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` = 0)of the RTL mode is the same as for fixed wing. It will fly to the nearest rally point (or HOME if no rally point is defined) and circle as a fixed wing aircraft about that point. The VTOL motors will not be used unless the aircraft drops below the airspeed defined in :ref:`Q_ASSIST_SPEED <Q_ASSIST_SPEED>`. The altitude the aircraft will circle at will be the altitude in the rally point, or the :ref:`RTL_ALTITUDE<RTL_ALTITUDE>` altitude if a rally point is not being used."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:36
#: 53e63c23313443c3919a00ab89d575ed
msgid "If in a VTOL mode when RTL is selected (either by a failsafe action or the pilot), the Quadplane will immediately transition to fixed wing and fly back as if in normal fixed wing RTL mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:41
#: 5321eea68c5343949c9c3b103a59862a
msgid "Hybrid RTL"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:43
#: 1995be138153404d8705494d8ca1b662
msgid "The another options for RTL in a QuadPlane are to fly as a fixed wing aircraft until it is close to the return point at which time it switches to VTOL QRTL mode and land vertically at the return point. To enable this type of hybrid RTL behavior you need to set the :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE <Q_RTL_MODE>` parameter to 1, 2, or 3."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:48
#: 914d50cc728f4bf385d4d54bc9ccd229
msgid "for the code to judge when to start the transition to VTOL in order to arrive at the point it should be totally VTOL, the :ref:`Q_TRANS_DECEL<Q_TRANS_DECEL>` parameter is used to calculate the when to start the transition. If the vehicle is overshooting, this value can be lowered, and vice-versa."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:52
#: 69843e7bd1fe4473baa97c05a55a2a58
msgid ":ref:`Q_RTL_MODE <Q_RTL_MODE>` = 1"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:53
#: d75977efe9234249a9c74f5deff3af7c
msgid "**RETURN FIXED WING, SWITCH TO QRTL, and LAND**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:55
#: 38959748ed4a421893845e814badc7bd
msgid "If in fixed wing mode when RTL is entered, the initial altitude that will be aimed for in the fixed wing portion of the hybrid RTL is the same as for a fixed wing RTL. You should set your rally point altitude and :ref:`RTL_ALTITUDE<RTL_ALTITUDE>` parameters appropriately to ensure that the aircraft travels at a safe altitude."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:60
#: 3843fd1576bc47acac10eb6e74418044
msgid "The distance from the return point at which the aircraft switches from fixed wing to VTOL flight is set using the :ref:`RTL_RADIUS<RTL_RADIUS>` parameter, or if that is not set then the :ref:`WP_LOITER_RAD<WP_LOITER_RAD>` parameter is used. The aircraft will then slow down as it approaches the return point, aiming for an altitude set by :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT <Q_RTL_ALT>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:66
#: 1fc39fa815a44b7fa8c4f986311fcbca
msgid "Once the return point is reached the aircraft begins to descend and land."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:68
#: f3cefc18b8a448b48aa3e759a5b507a9
msgid "If in a VTOL mode when RTL is selected (either by a failsafe action or the pilot), the Quadplane will immediately transition to fixed wing and fly back as if it had been entered while in a fixed wing mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:71
#: 85eb3ab125e04e6b96306ee028cbc36f
msgid ":ref:`Q_RTL_MODE <Q_RTL_MODE>` = 2"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:72
#: dede9a19021b4fcfa774c9d54e68e0dc
msgid "**RETURN FIXED WING, LOITER TO ALT, SWITCH TO QRTL, LAND**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:74
#: e52e617d0cbf437bac4287e032c44ca7
msgid "Setting :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` to 2 results in behavior similar to above, but with the vehicle returning like normal fixed wing RTL until it reaches :ref:`Q_FW_LND_APR_RAD<Q_FW_LND_APR_RAD>`, then loitering in fixed wing mode down to :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>` altitude, and then exiting facing the wind and executing a :ref:`QRTL<qrtl-mode>` to the home position. Be sure the loiter portion is set up to clear any obstacles."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:76
#: 2fc7310f11654ae8abf61e1d53a0ef57
msgid "If RTL is triggered within the larger of :ref:`RTL_RADIUS<RTL_RADIUS>` and :ref:`WP_LOITER_RAD<WP_LOITER_RAD>`, and below :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>`, in a VTOL mode or assisted fixed wing flight, the vehicle will proceed immediately toward :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>` and the landing position and then land (ie :ref:`QRTL<qrtl-mode>` mode)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:78
#: 36fb6fa4db6b4b1392aa1a4f56e585d7
msgid "If in a VTOL mode or assisted fixed wing flight when RTL is selected (either by a failsafe action or the pilot) beyond those radii, the Quadplane will immediately transition to fixed wing and fly back as if it had been entered while in a fixed wing mode."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:81
#: aa1ba58d3dde42c382bca8cb27c04744
msgid ":ref:`Q_RTL_MODE <Q_RTL_MODE>` = 3"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:82
#: a34b37e86225402bb037dce2fc95cc86
msgid "**RETURN FIXED WING,APPROACH TO VTOL TRANSITION POINT, AIRBRAKE, SWITCH TO QRTL, LAND**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:84
#: 100d8fcb14f9454ba600eb22a6ea0a28
msgid "Setting :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` to 3 results in behavior similar to a normal :ref:`QRTL <qrtl-mode>`. The vehicle will enter an \"APPROACH\" phase, and will return at :ref:`RTL_ALTITUDE<RTL_ALTITUDE>` and at a calculated distance, start a descent towards :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>`. As it approaches the landing position, ArduPilot starts an \"airbraking\" phase in non-tailistters to slow the vehicle and once slowed enters full VTOL mode and proceeds to execute a VTOL landing. This behavior is also used by default for the :ref:`QRTL<qrtl-mode>` mode unless :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 16 is set to prevent the Hybrid operation above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:86
#: 0f51ce614bec4721b70a0025dc57299f
msgid "In effect, this enables the QRTL mode for any RTL actuation: failsafe actions, mode change to QRTL, or completion of a mission (unless the last mission item prevents RTL)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:88
#: c7598ccdd0734478a4248e6caaacc58e
msgid "This mode is also used by default in all mission VTOL_LANDINGs unless the :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 16 is set to disable it."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:90
#: becbd8bd17554730bd5b3f944fc4dd16
msgid "This fixed wing \"approach\" allows VTOL landings to be used without needing to setting up approach waypoints to reduce altitude and get close enough to proceed in VTOL mode toward the landing point. If disabled by bit 16, the vehicle will instantly transition to VTOL mode upon that mission items execution, or upon mode changes to :ref:`QRTL <qrtl-mode>`, and navigate to its landing point in VTOL before doing a QLAND. This means that you should be very close to the landing site if the FW approach mode is disabled in a mission since it will proceed in VTOL flight to the land point."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:92
#: aa04fedc90744992accc8521ac7dad74
msgid "The image below details the phases of the approach and landing with the default setting of bit 16 (ie, not enabled):"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:97
#: 81f2bc2fe347441eb2ba376c4977644e
msgid "The phases of the approach are:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:99
#: 974ea9a3d3e84b11b2abc573735898dd
msgid "in a fixed wing mode when further than 2 times the greater of either :ref:`RTL_RADIUS<RTL_RADIUS>` or :ref:`WP_LOITER_RADS<WP_LOITER_RAD>` (MAXRAD) **plus** a calculated distance needed to descend from :ref:`RTL_ALTITUDE<RTL_ALTITUDE>` to :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>`, the plane will attempt to climb or descend to :ref:`RTL_ALTITUDE<RTL_ALTITUDE>`. If within that range, it will attempt to climb/descend to a linear descent slope, meet it, and continue to descend, as shown above."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:100
#: 0d0eb4eb218d48e6badf1dca5c4ad711
msgid "if started further than 2X \"MAXRAD\" but closer than above, at 2x MAXRAD it will continue in fixed wing mode at :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:101
#: c7fed9c90044441d970293d58c95b472
msgid "when it reaches a point that is within the VTOL stopping distance of the landing point (calculated using the VTOL deceleration parameter :ref:`Q_TRANS_DECEL<Q_TRANS_DECEL>` which gives the deceleration that will occur as the vehicle transitions to VTOL and the vehicle's current speed), it will transition to VTOL mode and send a message that it is in \"VTOL Position1\" and continue moving to the land point. If the vehicle is NOT a tailsitter, an \"AIRBRAKING\" phase may occur before the VTOL transition, spinning up the VTOL motors to create additional braking."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:103
#: c347f644529248a0a00fb12fdc3ea589
msgid "if the vehicle is overshooting \"VTOL Position1\", try decreasing  :ref:`Q_TRANS_DECEL<Q_TRANS_DECEL>` in steps. However, this increases the point before \"VTOL Position1\" that the vehicle will transition to VTOL."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:105
#: 0b475cfe15214847ad45867330b0f0d6
msgid "once the QuadPlane is within 5m of the land point and moving less than 2 m/s, it will send a GCS message declaring that it is in \"VTOL Position 2\", and final position itself over the land point and begin its landing descent, which will also be indicated by GCS messages"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:106
#: b8fccd817e9a43078a13d61827237b18
msgid "if the approach is entered less than 1.5X MAXRAD, it will immediately move to \"VTOL Position 1\" state, whether entered from fixed wing or VTOL modes, and move toward the landing site attempting to obtain :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>` as it does so."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:107
#: 42e3b2e6bc704073864aa3aa717ef6c3
msgid "if in VTOL mode at greater than 1.5X MAXRAD, the  vehicle will climb to :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>`, if below, then transition to fixed wing and start a normal fixed wing RTL, and attempt to navigate to home, executing the approach. The climb and turn toward the landing point will occur at even low altitudes as determined by :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT<Q_RTL_ALT>`, so the :ref:`FLIGHT_OPTIONS<FLIGHT_OPTIONS>` bit 4 for \"Climb before turn in RTL\" and/or :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 0 for \"Level Transitions\" might be worth considering for the fixed wing initial phases."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:109
#: 3ca1d5fd34934d11acf1f3803ec30d95
msgid "In cases where it is feared that using the approach feature may result in it being initiated too close to HOME due to the 1.5X MAXRAD distance being too close in VTOL modes, instead of using :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 16 to disable the feature entirely, the :ref:`Q_APPROACH_DIST<Q_APPROACH_DIST>` to increase the distance from HOME that the vehicle needs to be to transition to fixed wing and execute an approach,"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:112
#: 9ade28739a954636a6b2ad6bbe0b051d
msgid "QRTL Mode"
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:114
#: 043b25ce8eeb4fb8a15f5f1e84de21c8
msgid "By default, switching to :ref:`QRTL<qrtl-mode>` mode will act exactly as :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` = 3, above. However, if you prefer to do return to launch as a pure VTOL aircraft (like a multirotor would do) then you can use the :ref:`QRTL<qrtl-mode>` flight mode, but with :ref:`Q_OPTIONS<Q_OPTIONS>` bit 16 set in order to disable QRTL's default behavior (which is like the hybrid RTL described above with :ref:`Q_RTL_MODE<Q_RTL_MODE>` = 3). The vehicle will transition to VTOL flight, if not already in VTOL, and then fly at the :ref:`Q_WP_SPD<Q_WP_SPD>` speed towards the return point, at an altitude of :ref:`Q_RTL_ALT <Q_RTL_ALT>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:118
#: c20f483df9534788b687a1b10f229488
msgid "Once the return point is reached the aircraft will start a vertical descent towards the ground for landing. The initial descent rate is set by :ref:`Q_WP_SPD_DN<Q_WP_SPD_DN>`. Once the aircraft reaches an altitude of :ref:`Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT <Q_LAND_FINAL_ALT>` the descent rate will change to :ref:`Q_LAND_FINAL_SPD <Q_LAND_FINAL_SPD>` for the final landing phase."
msgstr ""

#: ../../source/docs/quadplane_rtl.rst:125
#: 0d1980d8d562464796970feb623696b5
msgid "In the final landing phase the aircraft will detect landing by looking for when the VTOL motor throttle drops below a minimum threshold for 5 seconds. When that happens the aircraft will disarm and the VTOL motors will stop."
msgstr ""
